                <head>No. 289.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gibbs to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima, Peru</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-05-07"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 7, 1884</date>.
                        (Received May 29.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 94]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: As Mr. Phelps left here the day after his
                    official reception, I doubt if he had time to communicate to the Department the
                    correspondence that took place on that occasion. I inclose copy of Mr. Phelps’
                    official note to this Government and the answer of Señor Urrutia, minister of
                    foreign affairs, with translation; also copy and translation of the answer of
                    the President to Mr. Phelps’ remarks.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>RICHARD GIBBS.</signed></closer>





